{%- comment -%}
  § 7 Abs. 3 UWG "at the time of collection" objection notice (GDPR remediation,
  TASK 2). Shown at the point of purchase — at the foot of the cart summary on
  the cart page AND in the cart drawer — so the customer is told, clearly and
  free of charge, that motion sports may LATER contact them about its OWN,
  SIMILAR products, and that they may object at any time. This is the mandatory
  SECOND limb of § 7(3) (the in-email notice already exists on the backend).

  ⚠ LAUNCH GATE + LAWYER REVIEW: this exact German wording MUST be confirmed by
  the lawyer before launch — do not treat it as final. The backend keeps § 7(3)
  marketing sends DISABLED until this notice is live; the operator flips that
  flag only once the wording is confirmed and live. The copy is phrased as a
  future possibility ("ggf. auch") and never presents existing-customer
  marketing as already active.

  The TWO legally-mandatory surfaces — the checkout contact/email step and the
  order-confirmation notification email — are NOT editable from this theme repo
  (no checkout.liquid, no Checkout UI extension) and must be added in Shopify
  Admin. See docs/backend-handoff/UWG_7_3_NOTICE_THEME_NOTES.md for the exact
  copy + placement. This cart notice is the in-repo reinforcement.

  Localization: rendered for every cart view. This is a German-market (UWG)
  notice; if you serve additional language markets and want to hide/translate it
  there, wrap the markup below in
  {%- if localization.language.iso_code == 'de' -%} … {%- endif -%}.
{%- endcomment -%}
<p class="ms-cart-uwg-notice text-xs md:text-sm text-foreground/70 mt-4">
  Wir verwenden deine E-Mail-Adresse ggf. auch, um dich über eigene, ähnliche
  Produkte von motion sports zu informieren (§ 7 Abs. 3 UWG). Du kannst dieser
  Nutzung jederzeit kostenlos widersprechen — eine formlose Nachricht an
  <a href="mailto:widerspruch@motionsports.de" class="underline underline-offset-2">widerspruch@motionsports.de</a>
  genügt.
</p>
